### 4. Data Transfer Object (DTO) Pattern

#### The Problem

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   Database Entity                       │
│   ┌───────────────────────────────────┐ │
│   │ - id (Long)                       │ │
│   │ - firstName (String)              │ │
│   │ - email (String)                  │ │
│   │ - passwordHash (String) ⚠️ SECURE│ │
│   │ - internalNotes (String) ⚠️ HIDE │ │
│   │ - lastLogin (LocalDateTime)       │ │
│   │ - ipAddress (String) ⚠️ HIDE     │ │
│   └───────────────────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │
          │ Serialize directly (BAD!)
          │
          ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ API Response                            │
│ {                                       │
│   "id": 1,                              │
│   "firstName": "John",                  │
│   "email": "john@example.com",          │
│   "passwordHash": "xj@#$%^..." ⚠️ LEAK│
│   "internalNotes": "..." ⚠️ LEAK      │
│   "lastLogin": "2026-05-21",            │
│   "ipAddress": "192.168.1.1" ⚠️ LEAK   │
│ }                                       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### The Solution

```
┌──────────────────┐
│ Database Entity  │
│ (Full data)      │
└────────┬─────────┘
         │
         │ Transformation Layer
         │
         ↓
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ DTO (Data Transfer Object)   │
│ {                            │
│   "id": 1,                   │
│   "firstName": "John",       │
│   "email": "john@...",       │
│   "createdAt": "2026-05-21"  │
│ }                            │
│ ✅ SAFE TO EXPOSE            │
└──────────────────────────────┘
         │
         │ JSON Serialization
         │
         ↓
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ API Response                 │
│ ✅ No sensitive data         │
│ ✅ No internal details       │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

**Implementation**:
```java
// Entity - Database Model
@Entity
public class User {
    private Long id;
    private String firstName;
    private String email;
    private String passwordHash;      // ⚠️ Sensitive
    private String internalNotes;     // ⚠️ Internal
    private LocalDateTime lastLogin;
}

// DTO - API Contract
public class UserDTO {
    public Long id;
    public String firstName;
    public String email;
    public LocalDateTime createdAt;
    // passwordHash, internalNotes NOT included
}

// Service - Transformation
@Service
public class UserService {
  
  public UserDTO findById(Long id) {
    User entity = userRepository.findById(id);
    return mapToDTO(entity);  // ← Transform here
  }
  
  private UserDTO mapToDTO(User entity) {
    UserDTO dto = new UserDTO();
    dto.id = entity.getId();
    dto.firstName = entity.getFirstName();
    dto.email = entity.getEmail();
    dto.createdAt = entity.getCreatedAt();
    // Sensitive fields not mapped
    return dto;
  }
}

// Controller - Public API
@RestController
@GetMapping("/users/{id}")
public ResponseEntity<UserDTO> getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
  UserDTO dto = userService.findById(id);
  return ResponseEntity.ok(dto);  // ← Secure
}
```

**Benefits**:
- ✅ Security: Hide sensitive fields
- ✅ Flexibility: API independent of DB
- ✅ Versioning: Different API versions easily
- ✅ Performance: Send only needed fields

